  <div class="q-head">Questions 1–13</div>

  <div class="q-sub">Questions 1–5</div>
  <div class="q-instr"><p>Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1?</p><p>In boxes 1–5 on your answer sheet, write</p></div>
  <div class="tfkey">
    <p><b>TRUE</b>  if the statement agrees with the information</p>
    <p><b>FALSE</b>  if the statement contradicts the information</p>
    <p><b>NOT GIVEN</b>  if there is no information on this</p>
  </div>
  <div class="q-item q-card ielts-listening-question-item"><strong class="ielts-listening-question-number">1</strong><span class="q-num">1</span><div class="q-body"><p>The early Spanish called the potato by the Incan name ‘Chuño’.</p><div class="opt"><label><input type="radio" name="practice_single_reading_39_1" value="TRUE" id="practice_single_reading_39_1_TRUE" autocomplete="off" aria-label="Question 1: TRUE"><span>TRUE</span></label></div><div class="opt"><label><input type="radio" name="practice_single_reading_39_1" value="FALSE" id="practice_single_reading_39_1_FALSE" autocomplete="off" aria-label="Question 1: FALSE"><span>FALSE</span></label></div><div class="opt"><label><input type="radio" name="practice_single_reading_39_1" value="NOT GIVEN" id="practice_single_reading_39_1_NOT GIVEN" autocomplete="off" aria-label="Question 1: NOT GIVEN"><span>NOT GIVEN</span></label></div></div></div>
  <div class="q-item q-card ielts-listening-question-item"><strong class="ielts-listening-question-number">2</strong><span class="q-num">2</span><div class="q-body"><p>The purpose of the Spanish coming to Peru was to find potatoes.</p><div class="opt"><label><input type="radio" name="practice_single_reading_39_2" value="TRUE" id="practice_single_reading_39_2_TRUE" autocomplete="off" aria-label="Question 2: TRUE"><span>TRUE</span></label></div><div class="opt"><label><input type="radio" name="practice_single_reading_39_2" value="FALSE" id="practice_single_reading_39_2_FALSE" autocomplete="off" aria-label="Question 2: FALSE"><span>FALSE</span></label></div><div class="opt"><label><input type="radio" name="practice_single_reading_39_2" value="NOT GIVEN" id="practice_single_reading_39_2_NOT GIVEN" autocomplete="off" aria-label="Question 2: NOT GIVEN"><span>NOT GIVEN</span></label></div></div></div>
  <div class="q-item q-card ielts-listening-question-item"><strong class="ielts-listening-question-number">3</strong><span class="q-num">3</span><div class="q-body"><p>The Spanish believed that the potato had the same nutrients as other vegetables.</p><div class="opt"><label><input type="radio" name="practice_single_reading_39_3" value="TRUE" id="practice_single_reading_39_3_TRUE" autocomplete="off" aria-label="Question 3: TRUE"><span>TRUE</span></label></div><div class="opt"><label><input type="radio" name="practice_single_reading_39_3" value="FALSE" id="practice_single_reading_39_3_FALSE" autocomplete="off" aria-label="Question 3: FALSE"><span>FALSE</span></label></div><div class="opt"><label><input type="radio" name="practice_single_reading_39_3" value="NOT GIVEN" id="practice_single_reading_39_3_NOT GIVEN" autocomplete="off" aria-label="Question 3: NOT GIVEN"><span>NOT GIVEN</span></label></div></div></div>
  <div class="q-item q-card ielts-listening-question-item"><strong class="ielts-listening-question-number">4</strong><span class="q-num">4</span><div class="q-body"><p>Peasants at that time did not like to eat potatoes because they were ugly.</p><div class="opt"><label><input type="radio" name="practice_single_reading_39_4" value="TRUE" id="practice_single_reading_39_4_TRUE" autocomplete="off" aria-label="Question 4: TRUE"><span>TRUE</span></label></div><div class="opt"><label><input type="radio" name="practice_single_reading_39_4" value="FALSE" id="practice_single_reading_39_4_FALSE" autocomplete="off" aria-label="Question 4: FALSE"><span>FALSE</span></label></div><div class="opt"><label><input type="radio" name="practice_single_reading_39_4" value="NOT GIVEN" id="practice_single_reading_39_4_NOT GIVEN" autocomplete="off" aria-label="Question 4: NOT GIVEN"><span>NOT GIVEN</span></label></div></div></div>
  <div class="q-item q-card ielts-listening-question-item"><strong class="ielts-listening-question-number">5</strong><span class="q-num">5</span><div class="q-body"><p>The popularity of potatoes in the UK was due to food shortages during the war.</p><div class="opt"><label><input type="radio" name="practice_single_reading_39_5" value="TRUE" id="practice_single_reading_39_5_TRUE" autocomplete="off" aria-label="Question 5: TRUE"><span>TRUE</span></label></div><div class="opt"><label><input type="radio" name="practice_single_reading_39_5" value="FALSE" id="practice_single_reading_39_5_FALSE" autocomplete="off" aria-label="Question 5: FALSE"><span>FALSE</span></label></div><div class="opt"><label><input type="radio" name="practice_single_reading_39_5" value="NOT GIVEN" id="practice_single_reading_39_5_NOT GIVEN" autocomplete="off" aria-label="Question 5: NOT GIVEN"><span>NOT GIVEN</span></label></div></div></div>

  <div class="q-sub">Questions 6–13</div>
  <div class="q-instr"><p>Complete the sentences below.</p><p>Choose <b>ONE WORD ONLY</b> from the passage for each answer.</p></div>
  <div class="q-item q-card"><span class="q-num">6</span><div class="q-body"><p>In France, people started to overcome their distaste for potatoes because the King put a potato <span class="ansbox"><span class="ielts-listening-question-item"><strong class="ielts-listening-question-number">6</strong><input placeholder="Answer" type="text" name="practice_single_reading_39_6" id="practice_single_reading_39_6_" autocomplete="off" aria-label="Question 6"></span></span> in his buttonhole.</p></div></div>
  <div class="q-item q-card"><span class="q-num">7</span><div class="q-body"><p>Frederick realised the potential of the potato, but he had to deal with the <span class="ansbox"><span class="ielts-listening-question-item"><strong class="ielts-listening-question-number">7</strong><input placeholder="Answer" type="text" name="practice_single_reading_39_7" id="practice_single_reading_39_7_" autocomplete="off" aria-label="Question 7"></span></span> against potatoes among ordinary people.</p></div></div>
  <div class="q-item q-card"><span class="q-num">8</span><div class="q-body"><p>The King of Prussia used a kind of <span class="ansbox"><span class="ielts-listening-question-item"><strong class="ielts-listening-question-number">8</strong><input placeholder="Answer" type="text" name="practice_single_reading_39_8" id="practice_single_reading_39_8_" autocomplete="off" aria-label="Question 8"></span></span> psychology to make people accept potatoes.</p></div></div>
  <div class="q-item q-card"><span class="q-num">9</span><div class="q-body"><p>Before 1800, the English people preferred eating <span class="ansbox"><span class="ielts-listening-question-item"><strong class="ielts-listening-question-number">9</strong><input placeholder="Answer" type="text" name="practice_single_reading_39_9" id="practice_single_reading_39_9_" autocomplete="off" aria-label="Question 9"></span></span> with bread, butter and cheese.</p></div></div>
  <div class="q-item q-card"><span class="q-num">10</span><div class="q-body"><p>The obvious way to deal with England’s food problems was to grow high-yielding potato <span class="ansbox"><span class="ielts-listening-question-item"><strong class="ielts-listening-question-number">10</strong><input placeholder="Answer" type="text" name="practice_single_reading_39_10" id="practice_single_reading_39_10_" autocomplete="off" aria-label="Question 10"></span></span>.</p></div></div>
  <div class="q-item q-card"><span class="q-num">11</span><div class="q-body"><p>The Irish <span class="ansbox"><span class="ielts-listening-question-item"><strong class="ielts-listening-question-number">11</strong><input placeholder="Answer" type="text" name="practice_single_reading_39_11" id="practice_single_reading_39_11_" autocomplete="off" aria-label="Question 11"></span></span> and climate suited potatoes well.</p></div></div>
  <div class="q-item q-card"><span class="q-num">12</span><div class="q-body"><p>Between 1780 and 1841, thanks to the widespread <span class="ansbox"><span class="ielts-listening-question-item"><strong class="ielts-listening-question-number">12</strong><input placeholder="Answer" type="text" name="practice_single_reading_39_12" id="practice_single_reading_39_12_" autocomplete="off" aria-label="Question 12"></span></span> of the potato, the Irish population doubled to eight million.</p></div></div>
  <div class="q-item q-card"><span class="q-num">13</span><div class="q-body"><p>The potato’s high yields helped the poorest farmers to produce more healthy food almost without <span class="ansbox"><span class="ielts-listening-question-item"><strong class="ielts-listening-question-number">13</strong><input placeholder="Answer" type="text" name="practice_single_reading_39_13" id="practice_single_reading_39_13_" autocomplete="off" aria-label="Question 13"></span></span> or hard physical work.</p></div></div>
