,"label":"The_History_of_the_Potato (2).html","reference":"The_History_of_the_Potato (2).html"}]},"explanations":{"1":{"part":1,"en":"FALSE — Paragraph A says the Spanish chroniclers “misused the Indian word batata (sweet potato) as the name for the potato”. Chuño was the name of the dried, preserved potato food, not the Spanish name for the plant.","uz":"FALSE — A paragrafida ispan yilnomachilari kartoshkani “batata” (shirin kartoshka) so‘zi bilan noto‘g‘ri atagani aytiladi. Chuño esa quritilgan kartoshka mahsulotining nomi, ispanlar bergan nom emas.","quotes":["misused the Indian word batata (sweet potato) as the name for the potato"],"ru":"FALSE — В пункте А говорится, что испанские летописцы «неправильно использовали индийское слово батата (сладкий картофель) в качестве названия картофеля». Чуньо — это название сушеного консервированного картофеля, а не испанское название растения.","translationProvenance":{"ru":{"type":"machine-translation","sourceLanguage":"en","provider":"Google Translate","sourceSha256":"90f566e81bb3ae9fcfb10d8109073d5c564fc6c91b0dcb89fbd79c3d12f10cfc"}}},"2":{"part":1,"en":"FALSE — Paragraph B: “The Spanish conquistadors first encountered the potato when they arrived in Peru in 1532 in search of gold.” They came for gold, and found the potato by chance.","uz":"FALSE — B paragrafi: ispan konkistadorlari 1532-yilda Peruga oltin izlab kelgan va kartoshkaga tasodifan duch kelgan. Demak, maqsad kartoshka emas edi.","quotes":["when they arrived in Peru in 1532 in search of gold"],"ru":"FALSE — Параграф Б: «Испанские конкистадоры впервые столкнулись с картофелем, когда прибыли в Перу в 1532 году в поисках золота». Они пришли за золотом, а картошку нашли случайно.","translationProvenance":{"ru":{"type":"machine-translation","sourceLanguage":"en","provider":"Google Translate","sourceSha256":"b10a6b482c57359b2efb7098bffd33993d86a1d32f0fa50a1b2a9c01ae124170"}}},"3":{"part":1,"en":"NOT GIVEN — The passage says potatoes were “generally considered to be unfit for human consumption” and that in England most vegetables were thought “nutritionally worthless”, but it never says the Spanish compared the potato’s nutrients with those of other vegetables.","uz":"NOT GIVEN — Matnda kartoshka odam yeyishga yaroqsiz deb hisoblangani aytiladi, ammo ispanlar uning tarkibidagi moddalarni boshqa sabzavotlar bilan solishtirgani haqida hech narsa yozilmagan.","quotes":["Generally considered to be unfit for human consumption"],"ru":"NOT GIVEN — В этом отрывке говорится, что картофель «в целом считался непригодным для употребления в пищу человеком» и что в Англии большинство овощей считались «бесполезными с точки зрения питательной ценности», но в нем никогда не говорится, что испанцы сравнивали питательные вещества картофеля с питательными веществами других овощей.","translationProvenance":{"ru":{"type":"machine-translation","sourceLanguage":"en","provider":"Google Translate","sourceSha256":"a92748c5fe6a98ec376e03fdca4e927d3dfe90e1951ae988b398cf235a01d2a1"}}},"4":{"part":1,"en":"TRUE — Paragraph B: “Even peasants refused to eat from a plant that produced ugly, misshapen tubers.”","uz":"TRUE — B paragrafi: hatto dehqonlar ham xunuk, shaklsiz tugunak beradigan o‘simlikni yeyishdan bosh tortgan.","quotes":["Even peasants refused to eat from a plant that produced ugly, misshapen tubers"],"ru":"TRUE — Параграф Б: «Даже крестьяне отказывались есть растение, которое давало уродливые, деформированные клубни».","translationProvenance":{"ru":{"type":"machine-translation","sourceLanguage":"en","provider":"Google Translate","sourceSha256":"1d4c20676b8dcb6261d6a563dc5effc4a451b3da03f4c5966079bac8c9e351a2"}}},"5":{"part":1,"en":"TRUE — Paragraph C: “Potatoes did not become a staple until, during the food shortages associated with the Revolutionary Wars, the English government began to officially encourage potato cultivation.”","uz":"TRUE — C paragrafi: kartoshka asosiy mahsulotga aylanishi uchun inqilobiy urushlar davridagi oziq-ovqat tanqisligi va hukumatning rag‘batlantirishi kerak bo‘ldi.","quotes":["during the food shortages associated with the Revolutionary Wars, the English government began to officially encourage potato cultivation"],"ru":"TRUE — Параграф C: «Картофель не стал основным продуктом питания до тех пор, пока во время нехватки продовольствия, связанной с войнами за независимость, английское правительство не начало официально поощрять выращивание картофеля».","translationProvenance":{"ru":{"type":"machine-translation","sourceLanguage":"en","provider":"Google Translate","sourceSha256":"ca40710956b2262eafb7cdffc78c0714ac957ddc7fa4ace494850822c64fb5dd"}}},"6":{"part":1,"en":"flower — Paragraph D: “Louis XVI began to sport a potato flower in his buttonhole, and Marie-Antoinette wore the purple potato blossom in her hair.”","uz":"flower — D paragrafi: Lyudovik XVI ko‘kragidagi tugma teshigiga kartoshka gulini (flower) taqib yura boshlagan.","quotes":["began to sport a potato flower in his buttonhole"],"ru":"цветок — Параграф D: «Людовик XVI начал носить цветок картофеля в петлице, а Мария-Антуанетта носила фиолетовый цветок картофеля в своих волосах».","translationProvenance":{"ru":{"type":"machine-translation","sourceLanguage":"en","provider":"Google Translate","sourceSha256":"41d03efd4b86c3fcca1995b10ee9f946492ca8b56a336203b37668a86d936307"}}},"7":{"part":1,"en":"prejudice — Paragraph D: Frederick the Great “saw the potato’s potential… but faced the challenge of overcoming the people’s prejudice against the plant.”","uz":"prejudice — D paragrafi: Buyuk Fridrix kartoshkaning imkoniyatini ko‘rgan, biroq xalqning unga nisbatan xurofoti va salbiy qarashini (prejudice) yengishi kerak edi.","quotes":["prejudice against the plant"],"ru":"предрассудки — Параграф D: Фридрих Великий «видел потенциал картофеля… но столкнулся с проблемой преодоления предубеждений людей против этого растения».","translationProvenance":{"ru":{"type":"machine-translation","sourceLanguage":"en","provider":"Google Translate","sourceSha256":"2568f74b7c4224bff50e1caef0c7a6648d9635dce57a8c130406c19b55c3ca2a"}}},"8":{"part":1,"en":"reverse — Paragraph E: “Trying a less direct approach… Frederick used a bit of reverse psychology: he planted a royal field of potato plants and stationed a heavy guard.”","uz":"reverse — E paragrafi: Fridrix teskari psixologiyadan (reverse psychology) foydalanib, kartoshka ekilgan qirol dalasini qattiq qo‘riqlashni buyurgan.","quotes":["Frederick used a bit of reverse psychology"],"ru":"обратная сторона — Параграф E: «Пытаясь менее прямым подходом… Фредерик использовал немного обратной психологии: он посадил королевское поле картофельных растений и разместил тяжелую охрану».","translationProvenance":{"ru":{"type":"machine-translation","sourceLanguage":"en","provider":"Google Translate","sourceSha256":"d509a1841bbeaaa04871320e8dc6b17a6851c12d3481850bd47ff2dbdf5f7bdd"}}},"9":{"part":1,"en":"meat — Paragraph F: “Prior to 1800, the English diet had consisted primarily of meat, supplemented by bread, butter and cheese.”","uz":"meat — F paragrafi: 1800-yilgacha inglizlarning taomnomasi asosan go‘shtdan (meat), qo‘shimcha ravishda non, sariyog‘ va pishloqdan iborat bo‘lgan.","quotes":["the English diet had consisted primarily of meat, supplemented by bread, butter and cheese"],"ru":"мясо — Параграф F: «До 1800 года рацион англичан состоял в основном из мяса, дополненного хлебом, маслом и сыром».","translationProvenance":{"ru":{"type":"machine-translation","sourceLanguage":"en","provider":"Google Translate","sourceSha256":"e2208dad45b4bf35306a7ad774877e6f69915f44993a12cd419fe6e27429d225"}}},"10":{"part":1,"en":"crops — Paragraph F: “High-yielding, easily prepared potato crops were the obvious solution to England’s food problems.”","uz":"crops — F paragrafi: hosildor va tez tayyorlanadigan kartoshka ekinlari (crops) Angliyaning oziq-ovqat muammosiga aniq yechim edi.","quotes":["High-yielding, easily prepared potato crops were the obvious solution"],"ru":"сельскохозяйственные культуры — Параграф F: «Высокоурожайный и легко выращиваемый картофель был очевидным решением продовольственных проблем Англии».","translationProvenance":{"ru":{"type":"machine-translation","sourceLanguage":"en","provider":"Google Translate","sourceSha256":"1600ed74a294273fc1e3a1fe8ccf38fe011a2d6098f655968b78735e925851f9"}}},"11":{"part":1,"en":"soil — Paragraph G: “The potato was well suited to the Irish soil and climate.”","uz":"soil — G paragrafi: kartoshka Irlandiya tuprog‘i (soil) va iqlimiga juda mos kelgan.","quotes":["The potato was well suited to the Irish soil and climate"],"ru":"почва — Параграф G: «Картофель хорошо подходит для ирландской почвы и климата».","translationProvenance":{"ru":{"type":"machine-translation","sourceLanguage":"en","provider":"Google Translate","sourceSha256":"1bddccdfe6f0fe65e055a4e7b8952091ce865aac97a86b3432f54e049cabf1d6"}}},"12":{"part":1,"en":"cultivation — Paragraph H: the population doubled “without any significant expansion of industry or reform of agricultural techniques beyond the widespread cultivation of the potato”.","uz":"cultivation — H paragrafi: aholi soni sanoat kengaymagani va dehqonchilik usullari isloh qilinmagani holda, faqat kartoshkaning keng ko‘lamda yetishtirilishi (cultivation) hisobiga ikki barobar oshgan.","quotes":["beyond the widespread cultivation of the potato"],"ru":"выращивание — Параграф H: население удвоилось «без какого-либо значительного расширения промышленности или реформы сельскохозяйственных технологий, помимо широкого выращивания картофеля».","translationProvenance":{"ru":{"type":"machine-translation","sourceLanguage":"en","provider":"Google Translate","sourceSha256":"514220819492bb07c06fbd5e7d89a106472c76900bb9ebeb6ee4b6155ed3b315"}}},"13":{"part":1,"en":"investment — Paragraph H: “the potato’s high yields allowed even the poorest farmers to produce more healthy food than they needed with scarcely any investment or hard labour.”","uz":"investment — H paragrafi: kartoshkaning yuqori hosili eng kambag‘al dehqonlarga ham deyarli sarmoyasiz (investment) va og‘ir mehnatsiz kerakligidan ko‘ra ko‘proq foydali oziq-ovqat yetishtirish imkonini bergan.","quotes":["produce more healthy food than they needed with scarcely any investment or hard labour"],"ru":"инвестиции — Параграф H: «Высокие урожаи картофеля позволили даже самым бедным фермерам производить больше здоровой пищи, чем им нужно, практически без каких-либо инвестиций или тяжелого труда».","translationProvenance":{"ru":{"type":"machine-translation","sourceLanguage":"en","provider":"Google Translate","sourceSha256":"c42beef4fe4b77fc66acd77ce6371b6fd1909497a3b64abf3a133978df4de0da"}}}}}]]
